      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T23:31:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, we still need this constructor since we don\u0027t currently have a constructor that exposes mPid or mUid (I\u0027m guessing we don\u0027t want to change that?). Also, we don\u0027t have a constructor that includes all both mPendingIntent and mMessenger/mBinder. \n\nI thought the above was the safest way to ensure the correct values were set while also not having to change the way we are calling the existing constructors in a bunch of other spots.\n\nThat said, I was able to simplify this Constructor now based off of your suggestion for nri.mNetworkRequestForCallback. In fact, making that changes has simplified code in a bunch of spots. It also helped me find a bug at l.8964 where I was checking the incorrect value for mNetworkRequestForCallback so thanks for suggesting the above! It would explain why a new unit test I am working on was having issues.\n\nI\u0027ll resolve this for now but feel free to reopen if you want to discuss further.",
      "parentUuid": "d66a862d_58cf3a5e",
